## 1. Dataset Selection Justification

### Source and Scope
I selected the **Bureau of Transportation Statistics (BTS) Airline On-Time Performance Data**. This dataset contains detailed records of domestic U.S. commercial flights, including departure and arrival times, delays, cancellations, diversions, and operational metadata. In addition to the core on-time performance dataset, I identified the **BTS Airline Carrier Lookup Table** as a related dataset required to resolve airline carrier codes into carrier names.

### Access Verification
The dataset is publicly accessible via the BTS website and is available as downloadable CSV files organized by year and month. I successfully downloaded sample data and verified accessibility by loading the data locally.

A sample of the retrieved data is shown below:

| FlightDate | Carrier | Origin | Dest | DepDelay |
|------------|--------|--------|------|----------|
| 2023-01-15 | AA     | DFW    | LAX  | 12       |
| 2023-01-15 | DL     | ATL    | JFK  | -3       |

Supporting evidence (CSV excerpt and access screenshot) is included in the `evidence/` directory.

### Relational Depth
The on-time performance dataset references several external entities via coded fields. One key relationship is between the `Carrier` field in the flight records and the carrier lookup table, which maps carrier codes (e.g., "AA", "DL") to airline names. These datasets can be joined on the carrier code to enrich flight records with descriptive airline information.

Additional potential relationships include airport codes (origin and destination) that may be joined with airport reference datasets.

### Temporal Characteristics
- **Update frequency:** Monthly
- **Historical depth:** Over 20 years of historical flight data
- **Time granularity:** Individual flight events with date-level granularity

This temporal depth enables both short-term operational analysis and long-term trend analysis.

### Why This Dataset
I selected this dataset due to its operational scale, rich relational structure, and relevance to real-world performance and reliability questions. Aviation data is inherently complex, and this dataset offers sustained analytical depth suitable for a semester-long architecture project.

